#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tacob — compile BOS to COB, decompile COB to BOS, and prove the round trip.

    tools/tacob compile   unit.bos -o unit.cob [-I dir]
    tools/tacob decompile unit.cob -o unit.bos           # or a stock unit: armpw
    tools/tacob dump      unit.cob [Script]              # opcode listing
    tools/tacob roundtrip --all [--out DIR] [--json]     # the landing-1 gate

BOS is the source and COB the build artifact (research/notes/tacob-design.md).
Formats: research/notes/file-formats.md §2. The code shapes below were
measured over the 278 stock COBs on 2026-09-07 and are what `roundtrip`
proves — every stock script decompiles to BOS that compiles back to the
identical file:

  * layout: header(44) · code · entry table · script-name table · piece-name
    table · strings (script names, then piece names, contiguous, no padding,
    EOF at the last NUL); header word 10 is the strings offset
  * every local is created at script entry (parameters first, `var`s after,
    hoisted); every script ends `PUSH k; RETURN` — the implicit `return (0)`
    is appended only when the last statement is not a return
  * literals truncate toward zero: <20> = 3640, <105> = 19114, <-100> = -18204
  * `get X` with no arguments is GET_UNIT_VALUE; with arguments it pushes the
    id and four arguments, zero-padded, then GET
  * operands are pushed trailing clause first: `turn … to D speed S` pushes S
    then D; `spin … speed S accelerate A` pushes A then S; `set V to E` pushes
    the id then E; `attach-unit U to P` pushes U, P, 0
  * `&&` / `||` evaluate both sides (no short circuit); unary minus on a
    non-literal is `0 - x`; no constant folding (`if( TRUE )` stays)
  * the stock corpus has no `else` and no forward JUMP; `else` is compiled the
    community way — `JNE else; then; JUMP end; else: …; end:`

Everything is stdlib-only. Reading stock units out of the game's archives
goes through `tools/ta3do`, loaded as a module the way tools/tascene does.
"""

